them separate (tests compare against independent brute force). Maybe debug assert off by default. Skip.\n\nComplexities documented: validation O(n² log n)-ish (Fraction gcd normalization), sweep O((n+k)·(n + log n · M)) where M bigint cost... document honestly: active list insert/delete O(n); each event does O(1) status mutations plus neighbor checks; total O(n log n) heap ops with Fraction keys; overall worst-case O(n² + k·n) plus log factors.\n\nTests (`tests/test_sweep.py`):\n- geometry unit tests: orientation signs, known intersections, fraction outputs, parallel-none, collinear touch, overlap detection.\n- rejection tests: vertical segment raises NotImplementedError; constructed triple-star raises NotImplementedError; collinear overlap raises NotImplementedError; degenerate zero-length ValueError.\n- handcrafted small scenarios with known answers: X crossing, T-touch, V-touch (endpoints), shared endpoints, collinear end-to-end touch.\n- Oracle: seeded RNG (random.Random(seed)), generate valid instance: sample segments with int endpoints in [0,25]; retry instance until validation passes (no vertical/triple/overlap). 200 seeds, sizes cycle 10..25. Compare set(find_intersections(segs)) == set(brute_force(segs)). Also assert result count reasonable? Just set equality.\n- 400-segment case: generate until valid (could take retries; concurrency rare, vertical rare; overlap rare-ish with range 0..50? overlap probability moderate; retry loop fine). assert counts equal (and sets equal).\n\nPerformance: 400 segments brute force O(n²) trivial. Sweep with Fractions fine. 200 instances × avg 17 segs trivial.\n\nGenerator:\n```python\ndef gen_instance(rng, n, coord_range=20):\n    while True:\n        segs=[]\n        ok=True\n        for _ in range(n):\n            while True:\n                p=(rng.randint(0,R), rng.randint(0,R)); q=(rng.randint(0,R),rng.randint(0,R))\n                if p!=q and p[0]!=q[0]: break\n            segs.append((p,q))\n        try: validate(segs)  # or catch NotImplementedError from find_intersections\n        except NotImplementedError: continue\n        return segs\n```\nValidation via exported `validate_input` function used by find_intersections; tests call it or just try find_intersections and compare after success.\n\nPackage layout:\n```\nsweep/__init__.py       (export find_intersections, brute_force_intersections, ...)\nsweep/geometry.py\nsweep/bentley_ottmann.py\ntests/test_geometry.py\ntests/test_bentley_ottmann.py\n```\n\nBuild iteratively with pytest at each step as requested. Let me start writing.\n\ngeometry.py:\n\n```python\n"""Exact geometric predicates ..."""\nfrom fractions import Fraction\n\ndef orient(a, b, c):\n    """sign of cross(b-a, c-a)"""\n    v = (b[0]-a[0])*(c[1]-a[1]) - (b[1]-a[1])*(c[0]-a[0])\n    return (v > 0) - (v < 0)\n\nNONE, POINT, OVERLAP = 0, 1, 2\n\ndef seg_seg_relation(p1,p2,p3,p4):\n    # returns (kind, point_or_None); inputs integer/Fraction coords\n    d1 = (p2[0]-p1[0], p2[1]-p1[1])\n    d2 = (p4[0]-p3[0], p4[1]-p3[1])\n    denom = d1[0]*d2[1]-d1[1]*d2[0]\n    if denom != 0:\n        rx = p3[0]-p1[0]; ry = p3[1]-p1[1]\n        t_num = rx*d2[1]-ry*d2[0]\n        s_num = rx*d1[1]-ry*d1[0]\n        # careful signs: solve p1 + t d1 = p3 + s d2\n        # cross(p3-p1, d2) = t*denom ; cross(p3-p1, d1) = -s*denom? let me verify.\n```\n\nDerive: p1 + t d1 = p3 + s d2 → t d1 - s d2 = w where w = p3-p1. Cross with d2: t (d1×d2) = w×d2 → t = (w×d2)/denom. Cross with d1: -s (d2×d1) = w×d1 → s (d1×d2) = w×d1 → s = (w×d1)/denom. Good: t_num = w×d2, s_num = w×d1, denom=d1×d2.\n\nIn 2D, w×v = wx*vy - wy*vx.\n\nt,s ∈ [0,1] check with Fractions: t_num/denom between 0 and 1 inclusive: multiply by denom sign-aware. Use Fraction(t_num, denom) then 0<=t<=1. Fine.\n\nPoint: x = Fraction(p1x) + t*d1x etc. Since inputs ints, could compute as Fraction(t_num*p1x... just use Fractions.\n\nIf denom == 0: collinear lines. Check overlap vs disjoint/touch. Since collinear, project on axis with